# Read this website with Python or the command line

Install Python 3.11 or newer. From this generated directory, run:

```sh
python3 -m pip install .
```

The generator's confirmed login is stored privately on this machine, outside this
package. By default, each website has a separate profile in the operating system's
user state directory. If generation used `--profile DIR`, select that same absolute
directory before calling this client:

```sh
export WEBSITE_CLIENT_PROFILE=/absolute/path/to/your/private/profile
```

Replace the profile example with your chosen directory. Leave this variable unset
when using the default profile. Profiles must belong to your user and allow no
access to other users. Credentials never belong in this package or its output.

Python reads return upstream generated models, whose fields are attributes:

```python
from $package import Client

client = Client()
$python_examples
```

The command line calls the same Python methods and prints JSON:

```sh
$cli_examples
```

These are examples. Replace `value` and numeric values with actual inputs from the
website. Command help lists required flags. Reads run without a browser or terminal
input. TLS certificates must be trusted by Playwright's request runtime.

A missing record raises `not_found (HTTP 404)`. Expired or missing login reports
`authentication_required`. To recover, explicitly sign in again:

```sh
printf 'Website login URL: '
read -r login_url
$name login --url "$$login_url"
```

Complete sign-in and MFA, then return to the terminal and press Enter when the
dashboard is ready. This renews the selected profile. Use `--browser chromium` or
`--browser-path /absolute/browser/path` to select an installed browser. The standalone
`python3 client.py login` command also works.

Reads never prompt for login, follow redirects or retry automatically. This public
interface supports captured same-origin GET operations returning JSON objects with
scalar query arguments. Other request shapes continue to use the upstream SDK.
